(# Technical Approach for SOE 2025 Azure Migration) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(## 1 Planning & Modernization) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 1.1 Discovery and Assessment) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Inventory & dependency mapping:** Use ASUK’s CMDB and Azure Migrate discovery tools to build a complete inventory of Windows Server 2016 hosts. Collect quantitative data \(SKU, CPU/RAM, applications installed\) and validate with application owners. Identify application dependencies and note any special servers \(e.g. jump hosts, SCCM, SonarQube\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Qualitative analysis:** For each application, record its tech stack, criticality, complexity and testing requirements. This helps prioritize applications for waves.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Application prioritization:** Together with ASUK, rank applications by strategic importance and risk. Select 3–5 non-business-critical workloads for a pilot.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Stakeholder & governance alignment:** Identify ASUK stakeholders \(architecture, security, change management\). Define maintenance windows, escalation paths and point-of-contact lists.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 1.2 Architecture and Wave Planning) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Landing zone design:** Create separate Azure subscriptions and resource groups for Dev, Test/UAT, Prod and DR. Use hub-and-spoke networking or VNET peering with subnets per tier, and apply NSGs and Azure Firewall.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Golden image creation:** Build a hardened Windows Server 2025 image in Azure Compute Gallery, including baseline agents \(Defender for Cloud, monitoring, backup\) and GPO settings.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Repository & package structure:** Follow the recommended repo layout: directories for environment config \(`/env`\), shared utilities \(`/common`\), instrument definitions \(`/im`\), datasets, ETL jobs and providers. Use camel-cased provider names and maintain a package descriptor with fields like group, name, version, description, components and requires.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Branching strategy:** Adopt Gitflow: develop features on `feature/<ticket>` branches, merge into `dev`, promote to `main` for UAT, and then to `prod`. Always include ticket numbers and squash commits.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **CI/CD pipeline design:** Implement Azure DevOps multi-stage YAML pipelines. Include build \(lint, tests\), plan \(terraform plan\), approval gates and apply stages. Add manual approvals between Dev, Test and Prod. Integrate style guides and code-quality scans.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 1.3 Modernization of Infrastructure-as-Code) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Terraform modules:** Develop reusable modules for VMs, networks and OS upgrades. Update them to reference Windows Server 2025 images and parameterize environment-specific details.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Parameterization:** Store environment-specific values in variables; keep secrets in Azure Key Vault; avoid hard-coding environment names.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Quality gates:** Run `terraform fmt`, `terraform validate` and `tflint` in the pipeline. Generate module documentation automatically. Enforce PR checklist items \(directory structure, manifest, scopes, comments and tests\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 1.4 Security & Compliance Planning) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Compliance alignment:** Map controls to APRA CPS 231/234. Enforce encryption at rest, RBAC and MFA. Document security architecture for ASUK’s review.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Baseline policies:** Apply Microsoft’s Windows Server 2025 security baseline and enforce via Azure Policy. Ensure GPOs reapply post-upgrade.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Security review:** Present detailed designs and pipeline code for ASUK’s security approval.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(## 2 Pilot Migration) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 2.1 Pilot Pipeline Development) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Upgrade pipeline:** Build an Azure DevOps pipeline that snapshots existing OS and data disks via Azure Backup, creates and attaches a Windows Server 2025 ISO disk from Azure Marketplace to each VM, runs an unattended upgrade using a PowerShell script executed by Terraform’s remote-exec provisioner, detaches the ISO disk, reboots the VM, and reapplies baseline configuration.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Configuration management:** Use PowerShell DSC or Ansible to enforce GPO, join domain, and install agents after upgrade.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Logging:** Capture upgrade logs in Azure Monitor; configure alerts for failures or extended duration.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 2.2 Pilot Testing & Validation) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Functional testing:** Verify application start-up, login policies, and key workflows.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Policy and security checks:** Confirm GPO compliance, Defender for Cloud recommendations, and overall security baseline.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Performance comparison:** Compare CPU, memory and disk metrics against pre-migration baselines; adjust VM sizes or disk types if needed.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Rollback verification:** Test the rollback plan by intentionally failing an upgrade and restoring from snapshots.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 2.3 Pilot Review and Improvement) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Conduct a retrospective with ASUK teams. Capture lessons learned; update Terraform modules, scripts and runbooks; obtain formal sign-off before full rollout.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(## 3 Full Rollout) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 3.1 Wave Planning & Scheduling) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Move group definition:** Use dependency mappings to group tightly coupled applications. Plan waves from least to most critical.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Communication:** Notify users and owners about maintenance windows and expected downtimes; obtain change-control approvals.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Capacity readiness:** Ensure Azure quotas and network resources are provisioned ahead of each wave.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 3.2 Wave Execution) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Pre-migration:** Freeze changes, back up VMs, update pipeline variables for target environment.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Migration:** Execute the upgrade pipeline across all VMs in the wave; monitor for failures.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Post-migration validation:** Run automated smoke tests and configuration checks; only enable production traffic once tests pass.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Wave sign-off:** Record results, update documentation and obtain owner approval before starting the next wave.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 3.3 Version Control & Release Management) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Maintain release branches tied to OS versions and tag each successful wave \(e.g., `v2025.1.0`\). Use squash merges and ticket numbers. Store Terraform state remotely to ensure consistency.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 3.4 Automation & Observability) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Pipeline templates:** Parameterize OS image IDs and environment variables; reuse templates across repositories.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Monitoring:** Deploy Azure Monitor dashboards to track upgrade status, VM health, and performance; set alerts for anomalies.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Reporting:** Generate automated reports summarizing upgraded servers, results \(success/failure/rollback\), and lessons learned.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(## 4 Stabilization & Hypercare) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 4.1 Hypercare Support) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Allocate a dedicated support team for at least two weeks post-wave. Use runbooks for common issues; integrate alerts with ASUK’s ITSM tool. Monitor performance and cost; right-size or auto-scale as needed.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 4.2 Knowledge Transfer & Handover) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Produce detailed runbooks covering upgrade pipeline, rollback procedures, and troubleshooting. Conduct training sessions for ASUK operations and DevOps teams.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 4.3 Security & Compliance Verification) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Perform final vulnerability scans \(Defender for Cloud\). Verify encryption, patching and privileged-access configurations. Provide compliance evidence to ASUK.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(## 5 Cleanup & Project Closure) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 5.1 Decommissioning) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Retire old Windows Server 2016 VMs after a grace period. Remove unused snapshots/disks and update the CMDB. Terminate any support contracts tied to old infrastructure.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(### 5.2 Documentation & Retrospective) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Compile a final report summarising the migration: number of servers upgraded, total downtime, issues and resolutions. Update architecture diagrams and IaC documentation. Conduct a project retrospective to capture improvements for future migrations.) Tj
0 -16 Td
0 -16 Td
(## Development Standards & Best Practices) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Coding conventions:** Follow PEP 8 for Python and Simon Holywell’s SQL style guide. Use uppercase SQL keywords and snake_case columns. Include headers in scripts \(Title, Description, Author, version\) and adopt Semantic Versioning.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Repo organisation:** Use the recommended repo structure with separate directories for configuration, common code, instruments, datasets and ETL jobs.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Pull-request checklist:** During code reviews, verify directory structure, manifest inclusion, scopes, comments and tests. Reviewers resolve comments inline and squash merges include ticket numbers.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **Branch naming & semantic versioning:** Use `feature/<ticket>-description`, `hotfix/<ticket>` patterns; maintain version numbers in modules and packages.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- **CI/CD strategy:** Employ multi-stage pipelines with manual approvals and integrate style checks and tests. Maintain distinct environments \(Dev, SIT, UAT, Prod, DR\) with clear networking and security boundaries.) Tj
